{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480923-entropy-and-vampires","id":1480923,"title":"Entropy and Vampires","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-05-12T21:25:58-07:00","id":1480923,"title":"Entropy and Vampires","content":"I am in a hybrid Vampire/Mage game and just got Entropy 4. I'm going down Entropy mostly for 5 for reasons. But I was wondering if Entropy 4 would be able to heal agg damage done to a vampire? It makes sense to me that it would. The book says Entropy 4 affects life (and can do agg damage), it doesn't specifically say it can also be used to heal, but that makes some degree of logical sense. Life in this sense seems like it would encompass a vampire, but it's ambiguous.<br /> <br /> We're pretty collaborative as a group, so I was just curious if there are any rules or house rules or thoughts on this so I can work with the ST to figure it out how we're going to handle Entropy and Vampires.<br /> <br /> - Also interested in combinations with other spheres for maximum effect. Especially with regard to vampires and... demons.<br /> <br /> As an FYI (I've mentioned this here before), this is an extremely long running campaign among friends currently in the dark ages. We are very strong - I have Arete 8 / Prime 6 / Mind 5 / Spirit 5... in addition to the Entropy 4. I only have Matter 2, so I'm also trying to avoid anything that requires high Matter.<br /> <br /> (Also, I know some people will be WTF - Arete 8? But this is our game, we're friends, this has been a long time. And the vampire i am trying to heal is 4th gen <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26423-lokitx","name":"LokiTX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-12T22:58:43-07:00","id":1480934,"title":"","content":"You do need Matter by the rules, but Matter 2 is generally enough to use a basic function of Life on a vampire, so I don't see why the same wouldn't apply to Entropy in this case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-12T23:34:22-07:00","id":1480939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiTX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480923-entropy-and-vampires#post1480923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am in a hybrid Vampire/Mage game and just got Entropy 4. I'm going down Entropy mostly for 5 for reasons. But I was wondering if Entropy 4 would be able to heal agg damage done to a vampire? It makes sense to me that it would. The book says Entropy 4 affects life (and can do agg damage), it doesn't specifically say it can also be used to heal, but that makes some degree of logical sense. Life in this sense seems like it would encompass a vampire, but it's ambiguous.<br /> <br /> We're pretty collaborative as a group, so I was just curious if there are any rules or house rules or thoughts on this so I can work with the ST to figure it out how we're going to handle Entropy and Vampires.<br /> <br /> - Also interested in combinations with other spheres for maximum effect. Especially with regard to vampires and... demons.<br /> <br /> As an FYI (I've mentioned this here before), this is an extremely long running campaign among friends currently in the dark ages. We are very strong - I have Arete 8 / Prime 6 / Mind 5 / Spirit 5... in addition to the Entropy 4. I only have Matter 2, so I'm also trying to avoid anything that requires high Matter.<br /> <br /> (Also, I know some people will be WTF - Arete 8? But this is our game, we're friends, this has been a long time. And the vampire i am trying to heal is 4th gen <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't have anything against the level of power of the members of your group, but I don't think I would allow a mage to heal a vampire with only Entropy 4. You'd need Matter, like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-13T21:34:17-07:00","id":1481044,"title":"","content":"I do have matter 2. So you'd say Entropy 4 Matter 2 would be sufficient to heal agg on a vampire?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26423-lokitx","name":"LokiTX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-13T23:20:48-07:00","id":1481048,"title":"","content":"I don't see why not. Entropy doesn't have to be destructive. You can use it to make things better too.<br /> <br /> Being a 4th dot effect means it's already not as good as using Life 3/Matter 2 (it has a higher min. and base difficulty so you'll heal less on average). I might slap on a 1 quintessence cost there depending on my intended mood for the game, but that really feels like the only reasonable restriction on how Entropy 4 is written up.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-14T14:58:34-07:00","id":1481132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480923-entropy-and-vampires?p=1481048#post1481048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see why not. Entropy doesn't have to be destructive. You can use it to make things better too.<br /> <br /> Being a 4th dot effect means it's already not as good as using Life 3/Matter 2 (it has a higher min. and base difficulty so you'll heal less on average). I might slap on a 1 quintessence cost there depending on my intended mood for the game, but that really feels like the only reasonable restriction on how Entropy 4 is written up.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You can't do it just with Entropy. You need at the very least Matter 2 to affect the vampire's pattern (in fact, one could go as far as to ask Life 5, but I, personally, wouldn't do it).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-14T15:02:51-07:00","id":1481133,"title":"","content":"Yes, like I said in post #2 of this thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-21T15:54:56-07:00","id":1481622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480923-entropy-and-vampires?p=1480934#post1480934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You do need Matter by the rules, but Matter 2 is generally enough to use a basic function of Life on a vampire, so I don't see why the same wouldn't apply to Entropy in this case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Errr... No. Healing a Vampire using Entropy would NOT require Matter 2.<br /> <br /> That would be like saying &quot;to heal a Vampire with Entropy 4, you also need Life 3. AND Matter 2&quot;.<br /> <br /> No. There seems to be a misunderstanding of what Entropy does.<br /> <br /> What is said about Vampires is that they are not fully living, but neither fully dead, but a sort of inbetween, THUS the need to use BOTH Life and Matter to heal (or any other change).<br /> <br /> Entropy 4 however ALREADY HAS THE CAPACITY TO ALTER MATTER. Hello! What is Entropy 3 by any chance?<br /> <br /> So no, if you use Entropy 4 to heal Vampires, that's all you need. The necessity for Matter 2 is ONLY if you're using LIFE 3.<br /> <br /> However, I personally request some 10 successes for each point healed that way, and the reason is simple, Entropy is NOT direct manipulation of the material, Entropy is the manipulation of PROBABILITY. Of chance, randomness, destiny, fate.<br /> <br /> With Entropy 4 you are NOT going to be mending the cells of the tissues back togheter, but rather increasing the odds of that happening by itself.<br /> <br /> Since Vampires dont have natural regeneration, one could say that Entropy 4 CANT do it - but it's Magik! And magik deals with the impossible.<br /> <br /> Thus, what such effect would do would be &quot;look! It's healing all by itself!&quot; or &quot;I'll be damned, it is healing by its own!&quot;. Much like you could use Entropy 3 to make a ruined rusted car to become brand new by reversing the physical entropy of it with a ton of successes, without actually being manipulating the matter (you are NOT removing oxygen atoms and reconnecting the iron atoms into the the metallic league, what you're doing is reversing the process which in real life physics is called &quot;entropy&quot;).<br /> <br /> So yes, you could theoretically heal Vampires using Entropy 4 (without needing ANY other Sphere), but I would require 10 successes for each point healed at least. That will depend on how powerful your ST wants Entropy to be, but if it can do anything than Life can (and Matter too by the way), then Life becomes useless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-21T16:41:49-07:00","id":1481627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480923-entropy-and-vampires?p=1481622#post1481622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Errr... No. Healing a Vampire using Entropy would NOT require Matter 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>If we're talking about pre-M20, I can understand the argument here, but M20 extends the concept of requiring additional spheres to target supernatural that are subject to multiple Spheres beyond the original side-bars around healing with Life (which hard already started previously).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That would be like saying &quot;to heal a Vampire with Entropy 4, you also need Life 3. AND Matter 2&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Not... really? It's saying the same logic that requires you to add Matter to heal vampires with Life applies to healing vampires with Entropy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What is said about Vampires is that they are not fully living, but neither fully dead, but a sort of inbetween, </div> </div> </div>That doesn't really explain why you need Mind to heal changelings. Nor does it address the logic presented in the locking on rules regarding these things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Entropy 4 however ALREADY HAS THE CAPACITY TO ALTER MATTER. Hello! What is Entropy 3 by any chance? </div> </div> </div>This feels too selectively literal for Mage. Taking control of a corpse like a puppet uses Life, but doing the same to bones is Matter... because the line between the two is blurry. Life can control &quot;matter,&quot; but not &quot;Matter Patterns.&quot; Entropy can similarly impact &quot;matter&quot; but not directly control &quot;Matter.&quot; By itself, Entropy can only makes things better/worse, not directly control them. Entropy can't fix a broken sword (even though it can break a sword) because swords don't naturally repair themselves. No amount of removing decay can undo the break. Vampires don't naturally heal either. Normally vitae is require to repair them. Entropy, by itself, could at most make vampire healing more efficient (but then locking on would require additional spheres anyway), just like it can make keeping a sword from breaking in the first place easier to do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However, I personally request some 10 successes for each point healed that way, and the reason is simple, Entropy is NOT direct manipulation of the material, Entropy is the manipulation of PROBABILITY. Of chance, randomness, destiny, fate. </div> </div> </div>What on Earth is the justification for requiring 10 successes per health level given the feats chart? Also, as noted, vampires are Matter associated patterns because, like matter, they don't heal naturally in a fashion that's controlled by randomness. Someone need to take a concrete action to heal a vampire (usually the vampire themselves). The probability of a vampire recovering health without a purposeful action to repair the damage is zero, not a value between zero and one that can be shoved in one direction or another. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> With Entropy 4 you are NOT going to be mending the cells of the tissues back togheter, but rather increasing the odds of that happening by itself. </div> </div> </div>... that's why we're saying it would take additional Spheres to heal vampires with Entropy, instead of just making it an obnoxiously difficult pure Entropy effect. Just as dead stuff it's Matter, not Life.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-22T05:54:47-07:00","id":1481654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480923-entropy-and-vampires?p=1481627#post1481627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If we're talking about pre-M20, I can understand the argument here, but M20 extends the concept of requiring additional spheres to target supernatural that are subject to multiple Spheres beyond the original side-bars around healing with Life (which hard already started previously).</div> </div> </div> </div>Which I absolutely do not agree on. So you're saying that if I want to Mind Control a vampire I need Matter too? What the hell is the sense in this? What if I throw a Time 4 to stop time in an area, is a vampire going to be unaffected because I didnt throw Matter in a nonsensical way in the mix?<br /> <br /> Mage has, particularly in M20, introduced many nonsensical and not well thought rules, like the need of Prime for Akashics to heal because they believe in &quot;Chi stuff... heal&quot;, when that should be just a fluff, and many other such.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480923-entropy-and-vampires?p=1481627#post1481627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not... really? It's saying the same logic that requires you to add Matter to heal vampires with Life applies to healing vampires with Entropy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which again makes no sense since Entropy already deals with (indirect) matter manipulation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480923-entropy-and-vampires?p=1481627#post1481627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That doesn't really explain why you need Mind to heal changelings. Nor does it address the logic presented in the locking on rules regarding these things.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the idea that Changellings are partly Mind pattern due to their dual existence as living and dreaming beings. Just as why you need Spirit for werebeasts because they are dual living and spiritual beings.<br /> <br /> That however should be restricted to changes to their patterns - ie any kind of &quot;metamorphosis&quot;. If I want to use Entropy 2 to make a werewolf trip on his toes or Correspondence 5 to make him being swallowed by the floor, it doesnt make sense to say I also need Spirit to do so.<br /> <br /> That's like saying that I need Life if I want to Mind Control a human being using Mind because he's a living pattern, or say that I need Matter to stop a bullet in the air using Time, because a bullet is a matter pattern. Again, nonsensical rules.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480923-entropy-and-vampires?p=1481627#post1481627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This feels too selectively literal for Mage. Taking control of a corpse like a puppet uses Life, but doing the same to bones is Matter... because the line between the two is blurry. Life can control &amp;quot;matter,&amp;quot; but not &amp;quot;Matter Patterns.&amp;quot; Entropy can similarly impact &amp;quot;matter&amp;quot; but not directly control &amp;quot;Matter.&amp;quot; By itself, Entropy can only makes things better/worse, not directly control them. Entropy can't fix a broken sword (even though it can break a sword) because swords don't naturally repair themselves. No amount of removing decay can undo the break. <br /> Taking control of a DEAD corpse cannot be done with Life. An argument could be made of either or not should you need Life WITH Matter to do so, or just Matter. I believe it's just Matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the case of vampires thou, they are NOT truly dead, just like they are not TRULY alive. Which is why you need BOTH. That's different of truly DEAD bodies.<br /> <br /> Entropy does NOT just &quot;makes thing worse/better&quot;. It CAN do things that would be highly unlikely or almost impossible. You could repair a broken sword with an ungodly amount of success, but it would be simply easier (and safer) to reforge it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480923-entropy-and-vampires?p=1481627#post1481627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires don't naturally heal either. Normally vitae is require to repair them. Entropy, by itself, could at most make vampire healing more efficient (but then locking on would require additional spheres anyway), just like it can make keeping a sword from breaking in the first place easier to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neither do rusted cars naturally &quot;un-rust&quot;, and yet you can do it with Entropy 3 anyway. Reversing entropy (the physics sense of it) is NEVER a natural process.<br /> But that's why Entropy is &quot;Magik!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480923-entropy-and-vampires?p=1481627#post1481627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What on Earth is the justification for requiring 10 successes per health level given the feats chart? Also, as noted, vampires are Matter associated patterns because, like matter, they don't heal naturally in a fashion that's controlled by randomness. Someone need to take a concrete action to heal a vampire (usually the vampire themselves). The probability of a vampire recovering health without a purposeful action to repair the damage is zero, not a value between zero and one that can be shoved in one direction or another.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I said before, rusted cars also dont naturally &quot;un rust&quot;, rusted cars also dont naturally &quot;heal&quot;.<br /> <br /> If you insist that vampires are &quot;matter patterns&quot; (which is nonsensical), I would say you can &quot;heal&quot; them with Entropy 3 alone. Or just using Matter.<br /> <br /> As for &quot;they dont naturally heal&quot; it doesnt matter because Entropy is about dealing with a bunch of &quot;unnatural&quot; changes, like &quot;un-rusting&quot; a rusted car. Or miraculously healing a terminal cancer.<br /> <br /> The need for 10 successes is that Entropy is NOT direct control. Using Entropy 4 to &quot;heal&quot; a normal human with few successes would at best increase his natural healing - just as you rightfully expressed about the vampire, making their own supernatural healing more effective (like allowing 2 health pts to be healed by each single pt of Vitae). For a miraculous &quot;insta heal&quot; you would need a ton of successes to do on a human instead of using Life to proper manipulate the flesh or without Life/Matter to properly manipulate undead flesh.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480923-entropy-and-vampires?p=1481627#post1481627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... that's why we're saying it would take additional Spheres to heal vampires with Entropy, instead of just making it an obnoxiously difficult pure Entropy effect. Just as dead stuff it's Matter, not Life.</div> </div> </div> </div>So why do you need to add Life to heal a vampire? Why cant you do it just using Matter?<br /> <br /> Again, and here I rest my case, that's a no brainer proposition. Mage is a game upon which each &quot;power&quot; (Sphere) is supposed to have a well defined &quot;realm&quot; of influence. The mixing of Spheres arent supposed to just be a random collection of different stuff based on the fickle flavours of it, but instead a well thought balance based of the realm of influence of each level. So, turning one stuff into another of another &quot;realm&quot;, requires different Spheres. Turning Spirit into Matter requires both Spheres. Making a Node have &quot;spasms&quot; of quintessence flows at random ways, require both Entropy and Prime (probably at 5 both). Saying however that you need Spirit AND Life to heal ANYONE because you're a Dreamspeaker that believes that &quot;everything is spirit&quot;, is nonsensical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-22T09:23:56-07:00","id":1481666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480923-entropy-and-vampires?p=1481654#post1481654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage has, particularly in M20, introduced many nonsensical and not well thought rules, like the need of Prime for Akashics to heal because they believe in &quot;Chi stuff... heal&quot;, when that should be just a fluff, and many other such.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that should just be an explanation for how their paradigm presents using Life to heal. I can see an argument being made for Akashics (and maybe Celestial Choristers) being able to alternately use Prime for healing by reversing the process of the Heart's Blood rote and converting quintessence into health levels, but that's an additional option, not a necessary requirement for the standard method.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-22T14:41:15-07:00","id":1481688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480923-entropy-and-vampires?p=1481654#post1481654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage has, particularly in M20, introduced many nonsensical and not well thought rules, like the need of Prime for Akashics to heal because they believe in &quot;Chi stuff... heal&quot;, when that should be just a fluff, and many other such.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not interesting in clogging up a thread about how to rule on a valid question someone has about applying the rules of the game wit ha debate about how you don't like the RAW.<br /> <br /> If you want to start a thread about your house rules, that's always an option.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-22T16:04:07-07:00","id":1481690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480923-entropy-and-vampires?p=1481688#post1481688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not interesting in clogging up a thread about how to rule on a valid question someone has about applying the rules of the game wit ha debate about how you don't like the RAW.<br /> <br /> If you want to start a thread about your house rules, that's always an option.</div> </div> </div> </div>Problem is, Im not so sure this is what it is in the RAW, or if it's the right interpretation - althought I'll give you the benefit of the doubt, since Im not entirely sure. I'll have to check it out (if you could do that it would be great, I'll need some time for it). If it is thou, oh well, what can be done. It's still nonsensical either way, but I wont argue if that's how it is written. The best I can do is to advice to ignore it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T21:46:15-07:00","id":1482345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480923-entropy-and-vampires?p=1481654#post1481654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which I absolutely do not agree on. So you're saying that if I want to Mind Control a vampire I need Matter too? What the hell is the sense in this? What if I throw a Time 4 to stop time in an area, is a vampire going to be unaffected because I didnt throw Matter in a nonsensical way in the mix?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not from what I can see, really.<br /> At least in M20 core, Matter for Vampires (And Mind for Fae, Spirit for Weres) is required anytime you'd want to normally affect or use a target's Life pattern - so, harming or healing the Life pattern.(Page 508) The only unclear thing would be Locking An Affect, which normally uses Life for people.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T01:43:32-07:00","id":1482352,"title":"","content":"In reading all of this, and as someone who excludes vampires from his Mage chronicle, I find it interesting to consider how I would interpret the rules if I included night folk in the story. If a player with high Entropy has a vampire ally, they want to be able to use it to heal them. Enemy vampire after their magic blood? - shred their pattern with the same sphere. It's intuitive to me to say that Matter would be required to affect the vampire's <i>body</i>. I<br /> <br /> If someone used a Time 4 effect to pause time, that would usually be a self-targeted spell. It's the Time Mage stepping out of the flow of time, rather than bringing the entire universe to a complete halt. The sphere-criteria for affecting the vampire don't count unless it's a version of the effect where the vampire experiences bodily paralysis - physical stasis that is imposed on every person and object in an area of effect. For that, I would say &quot;Matter Required&quot;. <br /> <br /> Now, I want to offer a comparative example. Let's suppose for a minute that someone is playing an Iteration X Bio-Mechanic and wants to cybernetically upgrade their vampire friend. I think I heard mention of something in canon lore that says vampires can't be cyborgs, but just suppose that wasn't true (if it is). Performing cybernetic surgery on a human subject requires both Matter and Life to integrate Enhancement and Recipient. If the Bio-Mechanic is working on their vampire friend, the sphere criteria are <i>reduced</i> from what it would be if they were operating on a human subject. <br /> <br /> What's happening in the operating room is that the surgeon-mage is fusing an object that was never alive with a body that is biologically dead. In this context, Matter as the required sphere simplifies life for the player. If the Surgeon only had the minimum Matter Rank (2) to enable combination effects on vampires using an applicable sphere they are more proficient in, they would be free to use the higher sphere's powers to effect the surgery. Entropy could easily apply to this.<br /> <br /> When we think of healing in the mundane world, surgery comes to mind, along with medication... and even meditation. A Life Mage with the luxury of time who wants to heal an injured human will often use some form of medicinal practice to channel their magic. Performing surgery is not uncommon among said healers. In a Mage setting with VtM crossover, Matter Focused healers, cyberneticists and bio-modders would be a thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T15:57:45-07:00","id":1482415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480923-entropy-and-vampires?p=1481690#post1481690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Problem is, Im not so sure this is what it is in the RAW, or if it's the right interpretation - althought I'll give you the benefit of the doubt, since Im not entirely sure. I'll have to check it out (if you could do that it would be great, I'll need some time for it). If it is thou, oh well, what can be done. It's still nonsensical either way, but I wont argue if that's how it is written. The best I can do is to advice to ignore it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> whole point is about making a <i>suitable</i> effect instead of debating how to do with Entropy alone.<br /> <br /> You said it yourself that you would require obscene amounts of successes using it. It is bending probability in a way that is possible only from a strictly quantum perspective, not 0, but so close to it to be effectively it for all intents and purposes.<br /> <br /> While this is fine and dandy, in practice requiring 10 successes to heal 1 Lethal is too similar to just saying &quot;no, you can't do it&quot;.<br /> <br /> Adding Matter in a combination effect ties it better to the Vampire's Pattern and makes for a far easier effect. Still not as good as Life + Matter, but still viable in game outside the most extreme circumstances.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T20:18:44-07:00","id":1482446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480923-entropy-and-vampires?p=1482345#post1482345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not from what I can see, really.<br /> At least in M20 core, Matter for Vampires (And Mind for Fae, Spirit for Weres) is required anytime you'd want to normally affect or use a target's Life pattern - so, harming or healing the Life pattern.(Page 508) The only unclear thing would be Locking An Affect, which normally uses Life for people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but Entropy isnt a Life Pattern manipulation now, is it? Entropy is a PROBABILITY/FATE/CHAOS manipulation, so Entropy 4 either 1) Can heal vampires alone or 2) cannot heal them at all.<br /> <br /> There's no middle ground here.<br /> <br /> In particular because Entropy 4 ALREADY have &quot;matter manipulation&quot; included by Entropy 3 - therefore you'd be just randomly adding unnecessary Spheres.<br /> <br /> Likewise, if we were to follow that line, you wouldnt be able to deny a player wanting to heal a vampire using Life 3 and Entropy 3 either, do you see?<br /> <br /> Entropy 4 is NOT &quot;Life manipulation&quot;, it's manipulation of PROBABILITIES inside of LIVING PATTERNS.<br /> <br /> And if Entropy 3 AINT matter manipulation either but PROBABILITY manipulation INSIDE MATTER PATTERNS, and if you tell me that &quot;vampires are a mix of Life and Matter patterns&quot;, then you MUST concede that Entropy 4 can ALREADY do BOTH.<br /> <br /> Either that or it CANT DO EITHER.<br /> <br /> This is an inescapable position.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T20:32:02-07:00","id":1482450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480923-entropy-and-vampires?p=1482446#post1482446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but Entropy isnt a Life Pattern manipulation now, is it? Entropy is a PROBABILITY/FATE/CHAOS manipulation, so Entropy 4 either 1) Can heal vampires alone or 2) cannot heal them at all.<br /> <br /> There's no middle ground here.<br /> <br /> In particular because Entropy 4 ALREADY have &quot;matter manipulation&quot; included by Entropy 3 - therefore you'd be just randomly adding unnecessary Spheres.<br /> <br /> Likewise, if we were to follow that line, you wouldnt be able to deny a player wanting to heal a vampire using Life 3 and Entropy 3 either, do you see?<br /> <br /> Entropy 4 is NOT &quot;Life manipulation&quot;, it's manipulation of PROBABILITIES inside of LIVING PATTERNS.<br /> <br /> And if Entropy 3 AINT matter manipulation either but PROBABILITY manipulation INSIDE MATTER PATTERNS, and if you tell me that &quot;vampires are a mix of Life and Matter patterns&quot;, then you MUST concede that Entropy 4 can ALREADY do BOTH.<br /> <br /> Either that or it CANT DO EITHER.<br /> <br /> This is an inescapable position.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please, just stop using all caps all the time to add emphasis and ending your posts with assertions that your conclusion is irrefutable or others' are nonsensical. Instead of improving your argument it is just making it annoying. Presentation makes a big difference.<br /> <br /> I'm not personally convinced either way and want to read the arguments, but I'm really struggling with these posts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T20:55:16-07:00","id":1482453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480923-entropy-and-vampires?p=1482415#post1482415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> whole point is about making a <i>suitable</i> effect instead of debating how to do with Entropy alone.<br /> <br /> You said it yourself that you would require obscene amounts of successes using it. It is bending probability in a way that is possible only from a strictly quantum perspective, not 0, but so close to it to be effectively it for all intents and purposes.<br /> <br /> While this is fine and dandy, in practice requiring 10 successes to heal 1 Lethal is too similar to just saying &amp;quot;no, you can't do it&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> Adding Matter in a combination effect ties it better to the Vampire's Pattern and makes for a far easier effect. Still not as good as Life + Matter, but still viable in game outside the most extreme circumstances.</div> </div> </div> </div>What it seems to me is that all of you just got stuck with &quot;healing requires Matter 2&quot; that you simply are not considering what each Sphere properly do.<br /> <br /> Yes, such an effect would have to be done practically on the level of quantum interactions. Adding Matter to it wont help thou. If the Vampire were made of clay it certanly would. However, Matter cant do ANYTHING on living Patterns, just as much as Life cant do ANYTHING with non metabolic matter.<br /> <br /> Sphere combination is done when:<br /> A) you want to &quot;combo&quot; several effects in a single one. <br /> - For example: adding Time 4 and Entropy 2 to create a conditional trigger. Time 4 places a &quot;delay&quot;, Entropy 2 introduces a &quot;condition&quot;. And, on top of that, you place some other Sphere with the thing that you wanted all along. For example, Life 2 for self heal. &quot;Self Heal (Life 2) held in delay (Time 4) until injury is suffered (Entropy 2). So, that's not really a single effect, but a &quot;combo&quot; of effects togheter in a single one.<br /> <br /> And<br /> <br /> B.) You want to change one Pattern that is governed from one Sphere into another Pattern governed by another Sphere<br /> - Example: Fireball (Forces 3, Prime 2). Prime 2, holding quintessence to be &quot;shapeshifted&quot; with Forces 3 into fire.<br /> <br /> The reason to use Life 3 togheter with Matter 2 is because vampires theoretically exist in a dual state between the two Realms, therefore you need both.<br /> <br /> Entropy 4 however DO NOT affect the LIFE Pattern - no more than Entropy 3 affects Matter Patterns or Entropy 5 Mind Patterns.<br /> <br /> What is does is controlling the PROBABILITIES on LIVING PATTERNS.<br /> <br /> Oh, it also control probabilities in Matter Patterns to by the way - because that was ALREADY a part of Entropy 3.<br /> <br /> Therefore, since Entropy 4 is NOT controlling ANY Life Patterns AT ALL (just the PROBABILITIES on LIVING Patterns), Matter cannot help AT ALL because Matter alone CANNOT control a vampire's body, right? And Entropy in this case is NOT helping Matter either, because Entropy is NOT controlling the Living Patterns either.<br /> <br /> If vampires are BOTH Life AND Matter at the same time, Matter alone cant do anything, because you need to manipulate Matter and Life pattern AT THE SAME TIME to do it - but Entropy 4 is NOT manipulating ANY Life Pattern AT ALL.<br /> <br /> And yes, this effect would boil down to manipulation of Quantum fluctuations to do it, which for me would require those 10 successes per HP, and wouldnt need Matter AT ALL.<br /> <br /> What you're saying is like using &quot;Life 3 Prime 2&quot; in order to &quot;heal better&quot;, theoretically because Prime 2 would &quot;control the Quintessence in the body &quot;better&quot; which is nonsensical since the flows of quintessence in organisms are in constant &quot;fluidity, and Life Sphere is already controlling this fluidity of Quintessence in order to heal, so adding Prime to this changes nothing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T21:17:31-07:00","id":1482457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480923-entropy-and-vampires?p=1482450#post1482450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please, just stop using all caps all the time to add emphasis and ending your posts with assertions that your conclusion is irrefutable or others' are nonsensical. Instead of improving your argument it is just making it annoying. Presentation makes a big difference.<br /> <br /> I'm not personally convinced either way and want to read the arguments, but I'm really struggling with these posts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didnt call other arguments nonsensical. I gave examples of nonsensical situations to illustrate a point.<br /> <br /> As for the caps, sorry, bad habit.<br /> <br /> As for saying my arguments are irrefutable, I aint wrong if Im right... Right? Lol. But I didnt say that my argument was irrefutable. I just used logical argumentation. As in &quot;if A equals B and B equals C, ergo A equals C, and that's unquestionable&quot;.<br /> <br /> Either way, if Entropy deals not with Life Patterns but with probability inside them, it cannot help Matter, because you'd still need life to act in union with matter.<br /> <br /> Lets do another example: imagine the vampire was made of &quot;conscious clay&quot;.<br /> <br /> In that case, Entropy 3 would do the trick, would it not?<br /> <br /> Note however that, in this case, we are not manipulating the vampire's clay matter, but rather the probability that his molecules would rearrange themselves in the ways they were before the damage.<br /> <br /> Therefore, there aint really any matter manipulation at all - just probability.<br /> <br /> Could I therefore combine Entropy 3 with Life to turn my clay vampire-boy into a &quot;real boy&quot;?<br /> <br /> No, because that would require actual transmutation of Matter into Life, which would require actual manipulation of the Matter Pattern, not just probabilistic manipulation. Therefore, I could not transmutate mattern into life using Entropy 3 and Life.<br /> <br /> Note however how this is exactly the same situation, just reversed.<br /> <br /> Which is why I stand by what I said.<br /> <br /> By the way, I do agree that you need Life 3 Matter 2 to manipulate vampires' bodies.<br /> <br /> I do not believe however that you can replace neither one for Entropy.<br /> <br /> Or do you really think that the mage could replace Matter with Entropy 3 for the exact same effect?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T04:51:53-07:00","id":1482480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480923-entropy-and-vampires?p=1482457#post1482457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didnt call other arguments nonsensical. I gave examples of nonsensical situations to illustrate a point.<br /> <br /> As for the caps, sorry, bad habit.<br /> <br /> As for saying my arguments are irrefutable, I aint wrong if Im right... Right? Lol. But I didnt say that my argument was irrefutable. I just used logical argumentation. As in &quot;if A equals B and B equals C, ergo A equals C, and that's unquestionable&quot;.<br /> <br /> Either way, if Entropy deals not with Life Patterns but with probability inside them, it cannot help Matter, because you'd still need life to act in union with matter.<br /> <br /> Lets do another example: imagine the vampire was made of &quot;conscious clay&quot;.<br /> <br /> In that case, Entropy 3 would do the trick, would it not?<br /> <br /> Note however that, in this case, we are not manipulating the vampire's clay matter, but rather the probability that his molecules would rearrange themselves in the ways they were before the damage.<br /> <br /> Therefore, there aint really any matter manipulation at all - just probability.<br /> <br /> Could I therefore combine Entropy 3 with Life to turn my clay vampire-boy into a &quot;real boy&quot;?<br /> <br /> No, because that would require actual transmutation of Matter into Life, which would require actual manipulation of the Matter Pattern, not just probabilistic manipulation. Therefore, I could not transmutate mattern into life using Entropy 3 and Life.<br /> <br /> Note however how this is exactly the same situation, just reversed.<br /> <br /> Which is why I stand by what I said.<br /> <br /> By the way, I do agree that you need Life 3 Matter 2 to manipulate vampires' bodies.<br /> <br /> I do not believe however that you can replace neither one for Entropy.<br /> <br /> Or do you really think that the mage could replace Matter with Entropy 3 for the exact same effect?</div> </div> </div> </div>The use of words like &quot;nonsensical&quot; and &quot;inescapable&quot; give a strong impression of ridiculing others' arguments and being extremely arrogant about your logic. It doesn't means that was your intent, just the impression given, but the caps add a lot on that impression anyway. I used to have that habit too, I know how it is.<br /> <br /> Otherwise this sounds already better and easier to think about (ain't communication a weird thing? How the form os a letter induces an emotional response and this response affects our comprehension?). I even re-read the M20 entry on Entropy and I agree with you, but actually wouldn't require so many successes, I'll get to that.<br /> <br /> Entropy <i>in the game </i>deals with decay, causing, halting or reversing it. We can go for a physics definition of entropy to explain decay, but that goes beyond the scope of the game for now. The thing is, by a common understanding of decay instead of the scientific definition of entropy, we're talking about &quot;natural&quot; decay, the slow &quot;degradation&quot; of a Pattern over time, instead of overt transformations through sudden interactions. I know this is nonsensical from a physics standpoint, but it is a necessary understanding for the game.<br /> <br /> With that, and re-reading, Entropy 3 alone can't revert damage on Matter. It affects Matter Patterns by affecting their decay on whatever form it takes on them, but it can't overtly repair damage. Would adding Matter 2 to it solve this? I don't know, depends on the Paradigm of the Mage, because &quot;grabbing&quot; the Pattern to target the individual fate of its components (like in a Quantum Healing) would conceivably be a Matter effect. That way, healing a Vampire with Entropy 3 would require all three Spheres discussed.<br /> <br /> But Entropy 4 adds another layer. It stands from level 3 on two things. One, it overtly affects Life Patterns on this regard, which certainly gives credence to your understanding. If it can affect Life at 4 and Matter at 3, it doesn't have any missing piece of the puzzle for Vampires. The second distinction, though, is that it <i>overtly states that it heals</i>. It simply does, and Aggravated, nonetheless.<br /> <br /> Going with this piece alone I'd say it doesn't have any reason to not heal damage as per the Base Damage or Duration chart, or very close to it. While the chart explicit says it applies just to healing from the Life Sphere, it is the default reference for any effect that is explicitly meant to deal or heal damage within the rules. We're not talking &quot;makeshift&quot; healing anymore.<br /> <br /> How to explain that? By myself I wouldn't say that Entropy can really mend things, but &quot;damage&quot; is a rather abstract concept. Cutting off your arm causes damage, but lacking the arm isn't the damage itself, never having it back won't keep you from completely healing. In a sense, damage isn't about how much you're wounded or chipped, but how much those wounds get you from a break down, which is an Entropic event. So healing with Entropy can be understood as reinforcing you against decay enough to keep that wound or missing piece from causing a &quot;catastrophic failure&quot;.<br /> <br /> \u200bIn any case, I'd say that the correct answer to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26423-lokitx\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26423\" data-vbnamecard=\"26423\">LokiTX</a> is that, by RAW, Entropy 4 is enough to heal any of their friends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T06:27:40-07:00","id":1482486,"title":"","content":"I'd like to chime in on this also. I'm not going to make a rules argument at this time, but I have read, digested, and considered this entire thread with interest and I would fall on the side of allowing Entropy 4 alone to heal a vampire. I do not really see any significant reason to require Matter or Life in this case.<br /> <br /> Also, it already has the penalty of being a rank 4 sphere rather than rank 3/2 (Life/Matter). This raises the difficulty over using Life 3, and includes additional paradox penalty for botching. Add to this that buying Entropy 4 from zero costs 58 xp, and buying Life 3 / Matter 2 from zero costs 52 xp, and in all ways Entropy 4 is not the preferred way to go on this. It *can* do it, but any mage with Life 3/Matter 2 available would choose that, and if the goal was to learn how to heal a vampire, the same mage would learn Life 3/Matter 2 before Entropy 4 if starting from zero in both cases.<br /> <br /> The point I guess is that not only do I think using Entropy 4 to heal a vampire is indeed an acceptable interpretation of RAW, but there is already sufficient penalty in place over the alternatives for anyone who plans to use it that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26904,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26904-breggie","user":"breggie","date":". 05-31-2022, 10:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26904-breggie","name":"breggie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26904_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T06:52:13-07:00","id":1482487,"title":"","content":"Agreed.<br /> <br /> I also don't think it should be <i>specially </i>difficult considering it's Adept level magick and whatnot. Using the &quot;damage table&quot; to determine success sounds fine to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">How to explain that? By myself I wouldn't say that Entropy can really mend things, but &quot;damage&quot; is a rather abstract concept. Cutting off your arm causes damage, but lacking the arm isn't the damage itself, never having it back won't keep you from completely healing. In a sense, damage isn't about how much you're wounded or chipped, but how much those wounds get you from a break down, which is an Entropic event. So healing with Entropy can be understood as reinforcing you against decay enough to keep that wound or missing piece from causing a &quot;catastrophic failure&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, I like this a lot. You're not so much &quot;regenerating&quot; the vampire, nor tampering with it's regeneration, as you're &quot;de-emphasising&quot; the wounds. Making them a non-issue. A very &quot;conceptual&quot; healing, I would say. A human could end horriby scarred by this. A vampire would regenerate the leftover &quot;wounds&quot; as with aesthetical modifications, I presume.<br /> <br /> I think this is one of these things where one would have to see how each Paradigm <i>makes</i> Entropy work as part of an individual effect. But I like it as an example of how Entropy could go about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-31-2022, 10:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T07:21:17-07:00","id":1482489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480923-entropy-and-vampires?p=1482487#post1482487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480923-entropy-and-vampires?p=1482480#post1482480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How to explain that? By myself I wouldn't say that Entropy can really mend things, but &quot;damage&quot; is a rather abstract concept. Cutting off your arm causes damage, but lacking the arm isn't the damage itself, never having it back won't keep you from completely healing. In a sense, damage isn't about how much you're wounded or chipped, but how much those wounds get you from a break down, which is an Entropic event. So healing with Entropy can be understood as reinforcing you against decay enough to keep that wound or missing piece from causing a &quot;catastrophic failure&quot;.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Also, I like this a lot. You're not so much &quot;regenerating&quot; the vampire, nor tampering with it's regeneration, as you're &quot;de-emphasising&quot; the wounds. Making them a non-issue. A very &quot;conceptual&quot; healing, I would say. A human could end horriby scarred by this. A vampire would regenerate the leftover &quot;wounds&quot; as with aesthetical modifications, I presume.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I like this concept also... It's a bit off topic, but maybe a good ruling would be that whenever being &quot;healed&quot; by Entropy, health boxes are temporarily removed. Maybe something like for every 2 or 3 health levels &quot;healed&quot;, one box is removed. For example, a fellow mage has 6 levels of aggravated damage, and you heal all of it with an Entropy effect. The &quot;damage&quot; is gone and they no longer have any wound penalties, but two health boxes are also removed, leaving only has 5 health boxes instead of 7. this persists until those two health boxes heal back naturally, and it may even leave permanent scarring.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that anyone *should* necessarily do this... just that I think it's an interesting concept about how using Entropy to heal is significantly different from using Life to heal.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26904-breggie","name":"breggie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26904_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T08:23:53-07:00","id":1482492,"title":"","content":"On that end, I would rather allow the character to ignore the penalties. Erasing the boxes it's quite harsh for such an effect, think that you can ignore all your wound penalties with one Willpower point.<br /> <br /> In general, WoD assume these penalties are more related to &quot;pain&quot; than to actual mechanical or biological impairment, that's why methods to endure or relieve pain will diminish, erase, or even transform them into bonuses (like with that Elder Auspex power).<br /> <br /> One could say that this is baloney, that such penalties should be much more than just pain at some point, but I would recommend to revise the HL system <i>itself</i> before taking in count more than that. I think this belongs with the &quot;death by stabbing your fingers 7 times&quot; territory, it's an issue of what the HL &quot;represent&quot; more than Entropy. <hr />Also I think what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> it's saying it's preciselly more across the line of avoiding death than anything else.<br /> <br /> Think about how in wars or accidents people can lose a lot of their body and not die, yet people can die from much less too (like, how suicide can be accomplished by two small cuts on the wrists).<br /> Think on the cases of people in war that even the medics <i>tought </i>were dead because of the insane amount of wounds from bullets, having &quot;tanked&quot; grenades that filled half their body with shrapnell, and yet &quot;somehow&quot; dind't die.Or like that one guy that had an iron pole trough the brain but was able to go to the medic, and didn't die.<br /> <br /> Entropy would get sure you're <i>one of those guys</i>, but won't give your legs back. May be wrong, but I think that's the gist of the Effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-31-2022, 11:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T08:52:05-07:00","id":1482495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480923-entropy-and-vampires?p=1482492#post1482492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...<br /> <br /> Entropy would get sure you're <i>one of those guys</i>, but won't give your legs back. May be wrong, but I think that's the gist of the Effect.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>So maybe instead of removing health boxes, it adds them. A mage with 6 levels of damage? They still have 6 levels of damage, but now they have 13 health boxes. Maybe distribute the new health boxes between everything except bruised, so they will always have a modifier though it will not be as bad as it would have been if they weren't &quot;healed&quot;. These additional health boxes last for the duration of the Effect, or until the wounds are otherwise actually healed.<br /> <br /> It may not be RAW, or is at best is an interpretation of RAW with some house ruling, but this would really differentiate Entropy healing from Life healing. Entropy &quot;healing&quot; would ultimately be gruesome and unpleasant, and it's only the Effect that is keeping death at bay - should the Effect end before the damage is healed for real, well....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26904-breggie","name":"breggie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26904_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T09:31:27-07:00","id":1482498,"title":"","content":"XD. Yeah, I tought that too.<br /> <br /> It's a bit bizzare. Someone that <i>was </i>closer to dying but now it's not w/o other apparent reason that the system &quot;decided&quot; it wasn't such a big deal after all ... My intuitions tells me that after massive bloodloss, or whatever that made you &quot;feel bad&quot;, your body should still need some sort of recovery (natural or not) after being &quot;healed&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T15:51:05-07:00","id":1482546,"title":"","content":"Yes, I meant something on those lines and some more.<br /> <br /> In reality &quot;damage&quot; doesn't kill you, not directly. What kills you are the consequences, and they vary a lot more than what the HL system measures, it is just an abstraction of how close you are from dying. A cut get's you closer to death because you bleed, your immune system is triggered, a lot of things in your body start to happen and they <i>may</i> lead to a collapse. And they may not. A newborn baby was once found alive in a trash bin with no less than 26 knife cuts in the body, pale due to blood loss, but alive. No vital organ or major blood vessel was damaged enough <i>to make it stop working</i>, and the blood loss was still below the fatal threshold. In my region a few years ago a robber was identified by locals, run to not be caught and... slipped in the wet grass, hit the only hard stone around and died almost immediately from the concussion. This is life.<br /> <br /> Entropic healing would deal with that. You're not bleeding so much anymore. The vessels that were about to rupture from stress are now starting to get better. Your immune system is picking the right anti-bodies quickly by dumb luck. The many changes inside your body that are what can actually kill you are going in a favorable route. Also, your body is strengthened by the spell, it isn't just a matter of what your current wounds are doing to you right now, but also that they don't mean new wounds will have an easier time killing you anymore, either.<br /> <br /> At the end of the day, 4 damage won't kill you, but it will make the next 4 kill you. If your body is strengthened enough for that to not happen, that's &quot;healing&quot;.<br /> <br /> But I do agree that, at the very least, an Entropy healing would rely on the spell duration to some degree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T16:31:42-07:00","id":1482550,"title":"","content":"Yeah, you would NOT want to have the duration of a healing based on Entropy expire before your body would have naturally healed the damage. Surprise! All those wounds you thought were no big deal anymore have suddenly started bleeding again and you're feeling very dizzy!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T19:07:26-07:00","id":1482560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480923-entropy-and-vampires?p=1482480#post1482480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The use of words like &amp;quot;nonsensical&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;inescapable&amp;quot; give a strong impression of ridiculing others' arguments and being extremely arrogant about your logic. It doesn't means that was your intent, just the impression given, but the caps add a lot on that impression anyway. I used to have that habit too, I know how it is.<br /> <br /> Otherwise this sounds already better and easier to think about (ain't communication a weird thing? How the form os a letter induces an emotional response and this response affects our comprehension?). I even re-read the M20 entry on Entropy and I agree with you, but actually wouldn't require so many successes, I'll get to that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, you are right indeed. When we are typing on a screen we seem to be less aware of that fact. THE BAD &quot;QUIRK&quot; of using caps is indeed a bad habit that is hard to forget... I just get caught in the emotion, and end up typing as the enfatic moments in my head come lol. I apologize, but thank you for the heads up. Indeed communication can get disturbed if we keep inducing emotional responses, even if we dont want to.<br /> <br /> As a human being, I have my flaws. &quot;Nonsensical&quot; is to try to use argumentation by exaggeration. For example &quot;Hitler was a vegetarian, so are we to assume all vegetarians are hitlerians?&quot; That's an absurd statement oviously. It's a way that Im very used to communicate which... Has never earned me much favors, let us put it that way. Still, old habits die hard, or so they say.<br /> <br /> Let us say that Charisma aint the attribute I spent most of my dots in, and leave it at that.<br /> <br /> Once again I apologize, but I hope I could pass my message well enough regardless of my lovable first impression","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T19:40:41-07:00","id":1482564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480923-entropy-and-vampires?p=1482546#post1482546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, I meant something on those lines and some more.<br /> <br /> In reality &amp;quot;damage&amp;quot; doesn't kill you, not directly. What kills you are the consequences, and they vary a lot more than what the HL system measures, it is just an abstraction of how close you are from dying. A cut get's you closer to death because you bleed, your immune system is triggered, a lot of things in your body start to happen and they <i>may</i> lead to a collapse. And they may not. A newborn baby was once found alive in a trash bin with no less than 26 knife cuts in the body, pale due to blood loss, but alive. No vital organ or major blood vessel was damaged enough <i>to make it stop working</i>, and the blood loss was still below the fatal threshold. In my region a few years ago a robber was identified by locals, run to not be caught and... slipped in the wet grass, hit the only hard stone around and died almost immediately from the concussion. This is life.<br /> <br /> Entropic healing would deal with that. You're not bleeding so much anymore. The vessels that were about to rupture from stress are now starting to get better. Your immune system is picking the right anti-bodies quickly by dumb luck. The many changes inside your body that are what can actually kill you are going in a favorable route. Also, your body is strengthened by the spell, it isn't just a matter of what your current wounds are doing to you right now, but also that they don't mean new wounds will have an easier time killing you anymore, either.<br /> <br /> At the end of the day, 4 damage won't kill you, but it will make the next 4 kill you. If your body is strengthened enough for that to not happen, that's &amp;quot;healing&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> But I do agree that, at the very least, an Entropy healing would rely on the spell duration to some degree.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. In never thought on HL on these terms. I as a ST always houseruled in disfavor of Entropy 4 for healing, because yes, I think that Entropy 4 is exactly as you and the others above were describing. Not miraculously making new cells grow out of nowhere like with Life 3, or if I want to heart attack someone, with Life 3 I simply close the main artery of the heart, as if it were a magic trick of telekinesis in it, but with Entropy 4 instead I make the fat of his body accumulate at his heart, increasing the already natural chance of that by 10x, 100x, maybe 1000x times over.<br /> <br /> Still, in my mind, a heart attack with Entropy 4 could be something of a matter of 10 minutes for someone with an unhealthy life style, to 2 years (instead of 50) to someone blessed with good genes and healthy habits. At least without a ton of successes that is.<br /> <br /> But now, interpreting HL as a simplification of &quot;system failure&quot;, it does indeed make sense.<br /> <br /> And yes, that's how Entropy works. Instead of &quot;healing&quot; exactly by &quot;glueing&quot; the ripped pieces back togheter as Life does, it instead modify the many random processes in the body... Instead of leaving it to chance, it gives a &quot;rush&quot;, making sure that the exact blood cell reached the exact bone cell to deliver the oxigen, and the proper hormones molecules &quot;swimming&quot; in the blood will reach the proper destinations in an optimized way... And doing that throughout the entire body, with every single cell, every single molecule, in a movement that, only by the natural physical interactions of the body, would take days, weeks or months to complete, but that however is synergized in such a way that takes seconds. That's how Entropy 4 would work in a &quot;scientific way&quot;.<br /> In game terms, for a Hermetic it would just be &quot;Vital Fortuna&quot;... No no, enough of this &quot;technocratic nonsense&quot; of &quot;quantum molecular probabilities&quot;, that's just &quot;techie mambo jambo&quot;.<br /> But irregardless of Paradigm, the notion is the same.<br /> <br /> PS: I love how in Mage I can sometimes find a better explanation for a mystical issue with scientific ideas, and some times scientific ideas are better explained with Mysticism. Forces for example is much easier to discuss using Science than the astrological motion of the planets, but Dimensional Science or Prime have to be explained using Mysticism and later &quot;translated&quot; into &quot;techno-babble&quot; lol that is a thing I noticed many years ago while thinking about the game and it never ceases to amaze me","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T21:03:55-07:00","id":1482571,"title":"","content":"This has been a great thread. It's given me a lot of new thoughts on Entropy, which I will be using in the future. I think we ended up using Entropy 4 Matter 2, but I did manage to successfully heal my methuselah friend before our impending battle with a demon of unknown power (which will probably occur sometime next week or the following). It's definitely made him much less nervous at a critical time, as we are attempting to gather allies to fight the demon (probably something stronger than an Earthbound, but we're not quite sure). We believe it has converted some of the powerful French vampires to its side and we're trying to turn Alexander and Demetrius into an ally against them.<br /> <br /> It's an amazing campaign and we're having a lot of fun. (I think it's like 1150ish and we're working to establish the Camarilla. Spent a lot of time with Hardestat.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26423-lokitx","name":"LokiTX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T04:03:25-07:00","id":1482585,"title":"","content":"Hum... Now that I thought of... This may be easier to explain under the &quot;technocratic scientific mambo jambo&quot; than under other Paradigms... Althought a Hermetic could explain it under &quot;harmonization of the body humors&quot;... Still, Paradigm could have an impact on wether or not this is possible","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}